To make BGP sessions more resilient to brief physical link issues, increase the BGP keepalive timer. This reduces the frequency of keepalive messages, giving the session extra time to recover during short interruptions. Here's the CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group "your-group-name"
        keepalive 90
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- Replace `"your-group-name"` with your BGP group name.  
- The value `90` sets the keepalive timer to 90 seconds (adjust based on your tolerance needs; valid range is 0–21845 seconds).  
- This extends the time BGP waits before considering the session down during intermittent link disruptions.  

For a specific neighbor, apply the command at the neighbor level instead:
```
configure router bgp
    group "your-group-name"
        neighbor "neighbor-ip"
            keepalive 90
        exit
    exit
exit
```
