To configure the BGP neighbor for IPv6 with a prefix limit of 5000 routes, a warning threshold at 75%, and logging without session teardown, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <your-group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            family ipv6
            prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 75 log-only
```

### Explanation:
- **`family ipv6`**: Enables IPv6 route exchange with the neighbor.
- **`prefix-limit ipv6 5000`**: Sets a maximum of 5000 IPv6 routes.
- **`threshold 75`**: Triggers a log event when the route count reaches 75% of the limit (3750 routes).
- **`log-only`**: Ensures the session stays up even if the route count exceeds 5000, while logging both threshold breaches and limit exceedances.

### Implementation Notes:
1. Replace `<your-group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP address.
2. The system will generate syslog messages when:
   - The route count hits 3750 (75% threshold).
   - The route count exceeds 5000 (full limit).
3. No session reset occurs on limit exceedance due to `log-only`.
